## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Connection Pooling Tuning

#### Current State
- [prisma.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/prisma.ts) creates a `PrismaPg` adapter with a bare connection string — **no pool sizing, idle timeout, or statement timeout** configured.
- [prisma.config.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/prisma.config.ts) references `DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED` for migrations (Neon pooler), but the runtime adapter has no explicit pool tuning.
- The PRD specifies connection pooling of 10–50 connections (NFR-PERF-005 Strategy).

#### [MODIFY] [prisma.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/prisma.ts)

Add explicit pool configuration to the `PrismaPg` adapter:
- `poolSize`: 20 (default pool, within PRD 10–50 range)
- `idleTimeoutMillis`: 30,000ms (release idle connections to save memory)
- `connectionTimeoutMillis`: 5,000ms (fail fast instead of hanging)
- `statementTimeout`: 10,000ms (kill runaway queries that exceed 10s)

This prevents connection exhaustion under load and ensures queries don't hang indefinitely.

