### 2. Database Query Optimization (Review Slow Queries)

#### Current State
- [dashboard-data.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/dashboard-data.ts) fires **8 parallel Prisma queries** in `buildDashboardData()` — this is already good (uses `Promise.all`). However, one of those queries (line 142–169) fetches **all assessments with all items and full control+framework relations** unbounded — no `take` limit. For users with many assessments, this is an N+1-at-scale risk.
- `getCachedDashboardData` (line 262) is a direct pass-through with **no caching** despite its name — the Redis cache module exists but is unused here.
- [assessment-score.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/assessment-score.ts) already uses optimized CTE+update SQL in the perf script, but the runtime `recalculateAssessmentScore` still uses two separate Prisma calls (fetch + update) instead of a single SQL statement.

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard-data.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/dashboard-data.ts)

1. **Add `take` limit** to the unbounded assessments query (line 142) — limit to most recent 50 assessments. Users with very large data sets don't need every historical assessment on the dashboard.
2. **Wire up actual Redis caching** via the existing `getCache`/`setCache` from [cache.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/cache.ts). Cache dashboard data for 60 seconds (short TTL since assessment updates should reflect quickly). This is the biggest win for repeated dashboard loads.
3. **Add `select` field narrowing** on nested `items` relation to avoid over-fetching columns we don't use.

#### [MODIFY] [assessment-score.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/lib/assessment-score.ts)

Add a `Prisma.$queryRawUnsafe` path that uses the optimized CTE query (already proven in [check-nfr.ts](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/scripts/perf/check-nfr.ts#L239-L283)) for the main `recalculateAssessmentScore` function when running outside a transaction. This keeps the framework-score breakdown computation from the existing Prisma path but makes the critical update atomic and faster.

