### 3. React Lazy Loading for Heavy Components

#### Current State
- **Zero** `next/dynamic` or `React.lazy` usage found across the entire codebase.
- The analytics page ([analytics/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/app/(user)/analytics/page.tsx)) imports the entire `recharts` library (51KB file, ~180KB+ bundled) — LineChart, PieChart, BarChart, etc. This is loaded eagerly even though users may never visit the analytics page.
- The remediation drawer ([remediation-drawer.tsx](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/components/ai/remediation-drawer.tsx)) is 10KB+ and imported statically in the checklist page even though it only renders when a user clicks "AI Remediation".
- The report components ([components/report/](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/components/report)) include 7 heavy sub-components imported statically.
- The onboarding page ([onboarding/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/app/(user)/onboarding/page.tsx)) is a massive 1,266-line file — the framework-selection sub-flow could be lazy-loaded.

#### [MODIFY] [checklist/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/app/(user)/assessments/[id]/checklist/page.tsx)

Replace the static `import RemediationDrawer` with `next/dynamic`:
