### 6. Bundle Size Analysis and Tree-Shaking

#### Current State
- The `package.json` does not have an `analyze` script.
- Lucide-react icons are imported individually (good — already tree-shakeable).
- recharts is a large dependency (~180KB) but only used in the analytics page.
- The onboarding page is 38KB+ of source in a single file.

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/package.json)

Add bundle analysis script:
```json
"analyze": "ANALYZE=true next build"
```

#### [MODIFY] [next.config.js](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/next.config.js)

Add conditional bundle analyzer integration:
```javascript
const withBundleAnalyzer = process.env.ANALYZE === 'true'
  ? require('@next/bundle-analyzer')({ enabled: true })
  : (config) => config;

module.exports = withBundleAnalyzer(nextConfig);
```

> [!NOTE]
> This requires installing `@next/bundle-analyzer` as a dev dependency.

#### [MODIFY] [query-provider.tsx](file:///c:/Users/zaidi/Downloads/compliance-dev%20(4)/compliance-dev/components/providers/query-provider.tsx)

Tune the React Query default `staleTime` from `0` (always stale) to `30_000` (30 seconds). The current `staleTime: 0` causes every component mount to trigger a refetch — even for data that was just loaded. This doesn't affect bundle size but reduces redundant network requests and re-renders significantly.

